p.src:
Krishnamurti does not choose among these alternatives. He asks whether there is an action that is not broken up, not contradictory, and not productive of further sorrow. The inquiry therefore changes shape: $\text{world disorder}
\;\longrightarrow\;
\text{what is one to do?}
\;\longrightarrow\;
\text{whole action}.$

