p.src:
The contrary assumption gives the old structure: $\text{observer} \neq \text{observed}
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\text{division}
\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
\text{conflict}.$ So long as there is division between observer and observed, conflict continues. When the observer sees that it is not separate from what is observed, the machinery of condemnation, justification, and escape no longer operates in the same way.

